 State the conditions under which your method is appropriate.", "competencyKeys": ["applied-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Invent a simple purchase or measurement problem represented by a two-step equation. Provide measurements or prices, explain the model and exchange your checked solution method with a peer.", "rubric": ["Interpret a solution in its context", "Record evidence and explain limitations"]}}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Reflection", "block_type": "synthesis", "sequence": 6, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Reflect on your independent response and practical task. Identify the evidence supporting your conclusion and one change that would improve the method. Let the distance be x kilometres. Solve 5 + 3x = 32 by subtracting five from both sides, then dividing both sides by three. The distance is nine kilometres; substitution gives thirty-two cedis.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Applied check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 7, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. A transport model charges a fixed five cedis plus three cedis per kilometre. The total fare is thirty-two cedis.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}]}, {"slug": "linear-equations", "depth": "advanced", "blocks": [{"depth": "advanced", "title": "Readiness check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 0, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. Two pricing rules are y = 5 + 3x and y = 11 + 2x. A learner says the second rule is always more expensive because its fixed charge is larger.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Complex scenario", "block_type": "big_picture", "sequence": 1, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Two pricing rules are y = 5 + 3x and y = 11 + 2x. A learner says the second rule is always more expensive because its fixed charge is larger.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Cross-concept connection", "block_type": "relationships", "sequence": 2, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Use the relationship between the relevant concepts rather than relying on a single recalled definition. Connect equations to graphs. State the assumptions needed for the connection.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Evidence evaluation", "block_type": "example", "sequence": 3, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Two pricing rules are y = 5 + 3x and y = 11 + 2x. A learner says the second rule is always more expensive because its fixed charge is larger.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Evaluate the claims and evidence in this scenario. Two pricing rules are y = 5 + 3x and y = 11 + 2x. A learner says the second rule is always more expensive because its fixed charge is larger. State one limitation and explain what further information would help.", "rubric": ["Solve unfamiliar multi-step equations", "Distinguish supported conclusions from assumptions"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Independent problem", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 4, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Two pricing rules are y = 5 + 3x and y = 11 + 2x. A learner says the second rule is always more expensive because its fixed charge is larger.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1", "advanced-2"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Find where the rules give the same cost, compare values on either side, and connect the equation solution to the intersection of two lines. Explain the meaningful domain for x.", "rubric": ["Solve unfamiliar multi-step equations", "Connect equations to graphs"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Challenge or investigation", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 5, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Two pricing rules are y = 5 + 3x and y = 11 + 2x. A learner says the second rule is always more expensive because its fixed charge is larger.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Design an unfamiliar multi-step equation problem with a contextual restriction. Solve it, justify each equivalent transformation, and explain how a mathematically valid solution could fail the context.", "rubric": ["Justify equivalent transformations", "Justify the method using evidence and stated assumptions"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Justification", "block_type": "synthesis", "sequence": 6, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Two pricing rules are y = 5 + 3x and y = 11 + 2x. A learner says the second rule is always more expensive because its fixed charge is larger.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1", "advanced-2", "advanced-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Defend the conclusions of your independent work. Explain the strongest evidence, address a plausible alternative and identify a limitation. Two pricing rules are y = 5 + 3x and y = 11 + 2x. A learner says the second rule is always more expensive because its fixed charge is larger.", "rubric": ["Solve unfamiliar multi-step equations", "Connect equations to graphs", "Justify equivalent transformations"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Advanced check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 7, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. Two pricing rules are y = 5 + 3x and y = 11 + 2x. A learner says the second rule is always more expensive because its fixed charge is larger.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}]}, {"slug": "graphs-interpretation", "depth": "applied", "blocks": [{"depth": "applied", "title": "Readiness check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 0, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. A rainfall table records ten, thirty, twenty and forty millimetres for four successive days. The class must compare the days and describe the overall pattern.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence 