2"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Use the rainfall values ten, thirty, twenty and forty millimetres to draw a suitable graph. Describe the pattern with numerical evidence and explain why the fall on day three matters.", "rubric": ["Compare datasets using graphs", "Choose a suitable representation"]}}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Lab or practical task", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 5, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Use measurements or representations to investigate the scenario. State the conditions under which your method is appropriate.", "competencyKeys": ["applied-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Collect or invent a small labelled dataset. Choose a representation, explain the units and scale, and answer two comparison questions from the graph.", "rubric": ["Interpret rate and change in context", "Record evidence and explain limitations"]}}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Reflection", "block_type": "synthesis", "sequence": 6, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Reflect on your independent response and practical task. Identify the evidence supporting your conclusion and one change that would improve the method. Label the horizontal axis with days and the vertical axis with rainfall in millimetres. Use equal intervals. Read the values before comparing them: day four has thirty millimetres more rainfall than day one.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Applied check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 7, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. A rainfall table records ten, thirty, twenty and forty millimetres for four successive days. The class must compare the days and describe the overall pattern.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}]}, {"slug": "graphs-interpretation", "depth": "advanced", "blocks": [{"depth": "advanced", "title": "Readiness check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 0, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. Two graphs show the same values, ninety-eight and one hundred, but one vertical axis begins at zero and the other begins at ninety-seven. A claim describes an enormous increase.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Complex scenario", "block_type": "big_picture", "sequence": 1, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Two graphs show the same values, ninety-eight and one hundred, but one vertical axis begins at zero and the other begins at ninety-seven. A claim describes an enormous increase.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Cross-concept connection", "block_type": "relationships", "sequence": 2, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Use the relationship between the relevant concepts rather than relying on a single recalled definition. Explain uncertainty and limitations. State the assumptions needed for the connection.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Evidence evaluation", "block_type": "example", "sequence": 3, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Two graphs show the same values, ninety-eight and one hundred, but one vertical axis begins at zero and the other begins at ninety-seven. A claim describes an enormous increase.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Evaluate the claims and evidence in this scenario. Two graphs show the same values, ninety-eight and one hundred, but one vertical axis begins at zero and the other begins at ninety-seven. A claim describes an enormous increase. State one limitation and explain what further information would help.", "rubric": ["Evaluate graph-based claims", "Distinguish supported conclusions from assumptions"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Independent problem", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 4, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Two graphs show the same values, ninety-eight and one hundred, but one vertical axis begins at zero and the other begins at ninety-seven. A claim describes an enormous increase.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1", "advanced-2"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Evaluate how the axis choice changes the impression. Calculate the actual difference, discuss what the data do and do not establish, and propose a clearer representation.", "rubric": ["Evaluate graph-based claims", "Explain uncertainty and limitations"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Challenge or investigation", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 5, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Two graphs show the same values, ninety-eight and one hundred, but one vertical axis begins at zero and the other begins at ninety-seven. A claim describes an enormous increase.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Compare two representations of the same dataset and an accompanying claim. Explain uncertainty or missing context, identify whether a causal conclusion is justified, and defend a fair summary.", "rubric": ["Connect multiple representations to justify a conclusion", "Justify the method using evidence and stated assumptions"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Justification", "block_type": "synthesis", "sequence": 6, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Two graphs show the same values, ninety-eight and one hundred, but one vertical axis begins at zero and the other begins at ninety-seven. A claim describes an enormous increase.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1", "advanced-2", "advanced-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Defend the conclusions of your independent work. Explain the strongest evidence, address a plausible alternative and identify a limitation. Two graphs show the same values, ninety-eight and one hundred, but one vertical axis begins at zero and the other begins at ninety-seven. A claim describes an enormous increase.", "rubric": ["Evaluate graph-based claims", "Explain uncertainty and limitations", "Connect multiple representations to justify a conclusion"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Advanced check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 7, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. Two graphs show the same values, ninety-eight and one hundred, but one vertical axis begins at zero and the other begins at ninety-seven. A claim describes an enormous increase.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}]}, {"slug": "photosynthesis", "depth": "applied", "blocks": [{"depth": "applied", "title": "Readiness check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 0, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. A class compares similar plants under different light levels while keeping plant type, water supply and observation time consistent.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Scenario", "block_type": "big_picture", "sequence": 1, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "A class compares similar plants under different light levels while keeping plant type, water supply and observation time consistent.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Method selection", "block_type": "process", "sequence": 2, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Choose the method by identifying the question, relevant quantities or observations, and an appropriate way to check the result. Identify light as the changed factor and choose an observable outcome. Keep other relevant conditions consistent, use repeated observations, and explain how the evidence relates to glucose production rather than treating soil as plant food.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Guided application", "block_type": "worked_example", "sequence": 3, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Identify light as the changed factor and choose an observable outcome. Keep other relevant conditions consistent, use repeated observations, and explain how the evidence relates to glucose production rather than treating soil as plant food.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Independent application", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 4, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "A class compares similar plants under different light levels while keeping plant type, water supply and observation time consistent.", "competencyKeys": ["applied-1", "applied-2"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Plan a fair investigation of light availability and photosynthesis. Identify the changed variable, measured outcome, controls and a prediction that could be challenged by the results.", "rubric": ["Interpret a photosynthesis investigation", "Explain effects of limiting factors"]}}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Lab or practical task", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 5, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Use measurements or representations to investigate the scenario. State the conditions under which your method is appropriate.", "competencyKeys": ["applied-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Interpret a teacher-provided plant investigation or carry out an approved classroom activity. Record observations, note limitations, and explain how light, carbon dioxide and water relate to the result.", "rubric": ["Use evidence to compare plant conditions", "Record evidence and explain limitations"]}}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Reflection", "block_type": "synthesis", "sequence": 6, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Reflect on your independent response and practical task. Identify the evidence supporting your conclusion and one change that would improve the method. Identify light as the changed factor and choose an observable outcome. Keep other relevant conditions consistent, use repeated observations, and explain how the evidence relates to glucose production rather than treating soil as plant food.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Applied check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 7, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. A class compares similar plants under different light levels while keeping plant type, water supply and observation time consistent.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}]}, {"slug": "photosynthesis", "depth": "advanced", "blocks": [{"depth": "advanced", "title": "Readiness check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 0, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. A dataset shows that increasing light initially raises the measured photosynthesis rate, but the rate later levels off. The carbon dioxide supply was not changed.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Complex scenario", "block_type": "big_picture", "sequence": 1, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "A dataset shows that increasing light initially raises the measured photosynthesis rate, but the rate later levels off. The carbon dioxide supply was not changed.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Cross-concept connection", "block_type": "relationships", "sequence": 2, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Use the relationship between the relevant concepts rather than relying on a single recalled definition. Connect photosynthesis to ecosystems and respiration. State the assumptions needed for the connection.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Evidence evaluation", "block_type": "example", "sequence": 3, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "A dataset shows that increasing light initially raises the measured photosynthesis rate, but the rate later levels off. The carbon dioxide supply was not changed.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Evaluate the claims and evidence in this scenario. A dataset shows that increasing light initially raises the measured photosynthesis rate, but the rate later levels off. The carbon dioxide supply was not changed. State one limitation and explain what further information would help.", "rubric": ["Evaluate experimental controls and limitations", "Distinguish supported conclusions from assumptions"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Independent problem", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 4, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "A dataset shows that increasing light initially raises the measured photosynthesis rate, but the rate later levels off. The carbon dioxide supply was not changed.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1", "advanced-2"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Analyse the plateau using limiting-factor reasoning. Propose another variable to investigate, state what the current evidence cannot distinguish, and connect photosynthesis with respiration or ecosystem energy transfers.", "rubric": ["Evaluate experimental controls and limitations", "Connect photosynthesis to ecosystems and respiration"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Challenge or investigation", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 5, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "A dataset shows that increasing light initially raises the measured photosynthesis rate, but the rate later levels off. The carbon dioxide supply was not changed.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Design a follow-up investigation to distinguish two explanations for a plateau. Justify controls, replication and measurements, and explain how the conclusions depend on the evidence.", "rubric": ["Analyse unfamiliar limiting-factor data", "Justify the method using evidence and stated assumptions"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Justification", "block_type": "synthesis", "sequence": 6, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "A dataset shows that increasing light initially raises the measured photosynthesis rate, but the rate later levels off. The carbon dioxide supply was not changed.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1", "advanced-2", "advanced-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Defend the conclusions of your independent work. Explain the strongest evidence,