", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Compare the solid's average density with water at approximately one gram per cubic centimetre. Discuss whether it would sink under the stated conditions, distinguish a hollow object from its material, and design a check of your prediction.", "rubric": ["Connect density to buoyancy with appropriate conditions", "Justify the method using evidence and stated assumptions"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Justification", "block_type": "synthesis", "sequence": 6, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "An irregular solid has a mass of one hundred and twenty grams. Water rises from twenty-five to forty cubic centimetres when the solid is fully submerged. The volume scale has finite precision.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1", "advanced-2", "advanced-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Defend the conclusions of your independent work. Explain the strongest evidence, address a plausible alternative and identify a limitation. An irregular solid has a mass of one hundred and twenty grams. Water rises from twenty-five to forty cubic centimetres when the solid is fully submerged. The volume scale has finite precision.", "rubric": ["Evaluate measurement error", "Determine the volume of an irregular object", "Connect density to buoyancy with appropriate conditions"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Advanced check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 7, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. An irregular solid has a mass of one hundred and twenty grams. Water rises from twenty-five to forty cubic centimetres when the solid is fully submerged. The volume scale has finite precision.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}]}, {"slug": "forces", "depth": "applied", "blocks": [{"depth": "applied", "title": "Readiness check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 0, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. A box is pulled with twelve newtons to the right while friction acts with five newtons to the left.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Scenario", "block_type": "big_picture", "sequence": 1, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "A box is pulled with twelve newtons to the right while friction acts with five newtons to the left.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Method selection", "block_type": "process", "sequence": 2, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Choose the method by identifying the question, relevant quantities or observations, and an appropriate way to check the result. Draw labelled arrows in opposite directions. Subtract five from twelve to find a resultant of seven newtons right. A nonzero resultant changes velocity; the diagram does not itself specify the current speed.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites":