nd practical task. Identify the evidence supporting your conclusion and one change that would improve the method. Draw labelled arrows in opposite directions. Subtract five from twelve to find a resultant of seven newtons right. A nonzero resultant changes velocity; the diagram does not itself specify the current speed.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Applied check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 7, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. A box is pulled with twelve newtons to the right while friction acts with five newtons to the left.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}]}, {"slug": "forces", "depth": "advanced", "blocks": [{"depth": "advanced", "title": "Readiness check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 0, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. A moving object follows a curved path at a constant speed. A learner argues that its forces must be balanced because its speed is constant.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent respo