-2"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Evaluate the argument by distinguishing speed and velocity. Explain the role of changing direction, connect your explanation to a force diagram and state what further information would be needed for a numerical calculation.", "rubric": ["Analyse unfamiliar interacting-force situations", "Evaluate evidence about force and motion"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Challenge or investigation", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 5, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "A moving object follows a curved path at a constant speed. A learner argues that its forces must be balanced because its speed is constant.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Compare two explanations for an unfamiliar motion observation. Design a measurement that could distinguish them, state assumptions about resistance and justify your model using evidence.", "rubric": ["Justify a model while stating its assumptions", "Justify the method using evidence and stated assumptions"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "title": "Justification", "block_type": "synthesis", "sequence": 6, "required": true, "objective": "Transfer and justify understanding", "content": {"body": "A moving object follows a curved path at a constant speed. A learner argues that its forces must be balanced because its speed is constant.", "competencyKeys": ["advanced-1", "advanced-2", "advanced-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Defend the conclusions of your independent work. Explain the strongest evidence, address a plausible alternative and identify a limitation. A moving object follows a curved path at a constant speed. A learner argues that its forces must be balanced because its speed is constant.", "rubric": ["Analyse unfamiliar interacting-force situations", "Evaluate evidence about force and motion", "Justify a model while stating its assumptions"]}}}, {"depth": "advanced", "tit