ect of opening the switch.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Method selection", "block_type": "process", "sequence": 2, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Choose the method by identifying the question, relevant quantities or observations, and an appropriate way to check the result. Trace the complete path through the source and components. Opening the switch breaks the only path and stops steady current. Use standard symbols and distinguish current from potential difference.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Guided application", "block_type": "worked_example", "sequence": 3, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Trace the complete path through the source and components. Opening the switch breaks the only path and stops steady current. Use standard symbols and distinguish current from potential difference.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Independent application", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 4, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "A simple low-voltage cell circuit contains a switch and two lamps in a single series loop. The class must predict and test the effect of opening the switch.", "competencyKeys": ["applied-1", "applied-2"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Draw and explain a simple series circuit with a cell, switch and two lamps. Predict what happens when the switch opens, and describe where you would measure current and potential difference.", "rubric": ["Build and interpret a simple circuit", "Use current and voltage measurements"]}}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Lab or practical task", "block_type": "application", "sequence": 5, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Use measurements or representations to investigate the scenario. State the conditions under which your method is appropriate.", "competencyKeys": ["applied-3"], "prerequisites": [], "task": {"prompt": "Use a teacher-approved low-voltage cell-and-lamp kit or a circuit simulation. Compare a series loop with two parallel lamp branches, record observations and avoid mains electricity or shorting the source.", "rubric": ["Investigate a circuit change safely", "Record evidence and explain limitations"]}}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Reflection", "block_type": "synthesis", "sequence": 6, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Reflect on your independent response and practical task. Identify the evidence supporting your conclusion and one change that would improve the method. Trace the complete path through the source and components. Opening the switch breaks the only path and stops steady current. Use standard symbols and distinguish current from potential difference.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": []}}, {"depth": "applied", "title": "Applied check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 7, "required": true, "objective": "Use the concept in context", "content": {"body": "Check your readiness to use evidence and explain a method. A simple low-voltage cell circuit contains a switch and two lamps in a single series loop. The class must predict and test the effect of opening the switch.", "competencyKeys": [], "prerequisites": [], "quickCheck": {"prompt": "Which response best supports a defensible conclusion in this scenario?", "options": ["Explain the method, use relevant evidence and state limitations", "Give a conclusion without connecting it to evidence"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "A conclusion needs an appropriate method, relevant evidence and clear limits. Your independent responses are assessed separately."}}}]}, {"slug": "electricity", "depth": "advanced", "blocks": [{"depth": "advanced", "title": "Readiness check", "block_type": "quick_check", "sequence": 0,